  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - No additional flank windows or other glazed openings shall be formed in the ___north  and south  elevation of units 1-4 and east and west elevations of units 5-6_________ hereby approved without the prior written consent of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 2 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 3 - The development shall not be occupied until screen planting along _the south and west____ boundaries have been planted in accordance with a scheme submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority in writing.",
    "Condition : 4 - No development shall take place until there has been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority a plan indicating the positions, design, materials and type of boundary treatment to be erected.  The boundary treatment shall be completed before (the use hereby permitted is commenced) or (before the building(s) is/are occupied) or (in accordance with a timetable agreed in writing with the local planning authority).  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 5 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on thesite except between the hours of  8.00am           to    6.00pm         on Mondays to Friday and   8.00 am        to     1.00pm      on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and public holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - The windows formed in the ___south elevation of units 1-4 and west elevation of units 5-6___________  shall be obscure glazed, hinged to open inwards and shall not be repaired or replaced otherwise than with obscured glazing.",
    "Condition : 7 - The refuse storage arrangements shown on the approved drawing shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 8 - No [dwelling] shall be occupied until that part of the service road which provides access to it has been constructed in accordance with the approved plans",
    "Condition : 9 - Before commencement of operations, a scheme shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority to cover the following matters:\r\n\r\n(i)\tany external illumination of the site\r\n\r\n(ii)\tmeasures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site; and\r\n\r\n(iii)\tmeasures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties.\r\n\r\nThe scheme so approved should be fully implemented.\r\n",
    "Condition : 10 - The use hereby permitted for __residential______________ purpose shall not be begun until full particulars and details of a scheme to insulate the premises against the transmission of airborne and impact sound has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and the development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given.",
    "Condition : 11 - The garage or car parking accommodation shown on drawing No. __100F received 5.2.2001_________ shall be provided before the dwelling to which it relates is occupied and thereafter it shall not be used for any purpose other than the parking of vehicles.",
    "Condition : 12 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 13 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority (before the building(s)are occupied)."
  ],
